# Video tab at this Mac's Recommended (a fresh test copy with DM_TEST_VIDEO_FIRSTBOOT=1: full screen, this Mac's own Recommended):
# the controller steps Graphic Presets to Quality, which must stay shown (on an M6 at 2560 x 1440 Recommended equals Quality),
# Discard drops it, then Performance is applied (dm_video.c: dm_video_pump, apply_preset and AcceptChanges with live selectors).
# The selection frame starts on the first Video-tab row when the page appears; the Mac rows are mode, res, color, preset, so three DOWN presses reach
# Graphic Presets (a video_row event naming another row means the row order changed). RIGHT steps the options; Custom is skipped while disabled.
# A test copy already runs the controller layouts (no padmode event follows inputmode). msg sends the same OptionsPanelMessage the page's buttons send. The screenshot is a second, visual check: the row must read Quality
name video_presets_mac
requires mac-app
save warlock
env DM_TEST_VIDEO_FIRSTBOOT=1
timeout 240

enter_game
sleep 3
open_pause
tap_ui Settings
sleep 2
inputmode mode=controller
sleep 1
press DOWN
press DOWN
press DOWN
press RIGHT
sleep 0.5
press RIGHT
sleep 1
screenshot video_quality.png
msg OptionsPanelMessage:CancelChanges
sleep 1
press RIGHT
sleep 1
msg OptionsPanelMessage:AcceptChanges
sleep 1
quit
check event picture how=first res=3 up=1 envsh=1
check event video_row row=preset value=1 preset=1
check event video_row row=preset value=2 preset=2
check event picture how=apply res=0 up=1 aa=0 envsh=0 shq=0
check no_red
check no_red_log
